home, it’s vital to watch your own health"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/33-05"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["05"]},"For long‑term wheelchair users, switch to a pressure‑relieving cushion and check the ischial and sacrococcygeal areas daily"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/33-06"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["06"]},"Don’t buy therapies or devices that claim to cure paralysis, blindness, or deafness"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/33-07"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["07"]},"After obtaining the disability certificate, visit the county-level civil affairs bureau to ask about all available benefits at once"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/33-08"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["08"]},"For children under 7 who have disabilities or autism, apply to the county-level civil affairs bureau for rehabilitation assistance"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/33-09"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["09"]},"Families can apply to local civil affairs bureaus at or above the county level for subsidies to modify ramps, handrails, and bathrooms at home"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/33-10"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["10"]},"Mentioning your disability certificate during a job interview can save the employer money"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/33-11"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["11"]},"Tax reductions for individuals with disabilities – how much can be saved? Call your provincial tax bureau for details"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/33-12"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["12"]},"Guide dogs are allowed in public places and on public transport; blind individuals ride city buses for free"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"aria-current":"page","className":"active","href":"/en/tip/33-13","data-status":"active"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["13"]},"Disabled candidates taking the national college entrance exam can request reasonable accommodations, including a 50% time extension for those using Braille test papers"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/33-14"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["14"]},"Schools may not refuse enrollment for children with disabilities; those unable to attend receive in‑home instruction arranged by the education bureau"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/33-15"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["15"]},"People missing their right lower limb or both lower limbs can still obtain a driver’s license; the designated category is C5"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/33-16"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["16"]},"Rehabilitation should be carried out at a proper facility with a rehabilitation medicine department; the intensity must be set by therapists — more intensity does not necessarily mean better results"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/33-17"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["17"]},"Getting a hearing aid when hearing declines — the reason is to hear better now, not to prevent dementia"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/33-18"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["18"]},"Saying an adult “can’t manage his own affairs” requires a court determination; family members can’t decide on their own"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/33-19"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["19"]},"Guardians for adults are appointed in a legal order; if the ward injures someone, the guardian must pay compensation"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/33-20"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["20"]},"If you’re denied a job, denied promotion, or paid less because of a disability, you can sue — but first calculate the associated costs"]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-tip-page"},"children":[{"tag":"nav","props":{"className":"life-tip-breadcrumb","aria-label":"Breadcrumb"},"children":[{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/book"},"children":["Explore the book"]},{"tag":"span","props":{"aria-hidden":"true"},"children":["/"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/book/33"},"children":["Chapter 33"," ·"," ","How to live after becoming disabled"]}]},{"tag":"article","props":{"className":"life-entry-card status-unmarked is-standalone","id":"33-13"},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-top"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-entry-number"},"children":["13"]},{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-evidence grade-a"},"children":["Evidence"," ","A"]}]},{"tag":"h1","props":{"lang":"en"},"children":["Disabled candidates taking the national college entrance exam can request reasonable accommodations, including a 50% time extension for those using Braille test papers"]},{"tag":"p","props":{"lang":"en","className":"life-entry-summary"},"children":["The Ministry of Education and the China Disabled Persons’ Federation have issued official guidelines outlining specific accommodations for disabled students taking the college entrance exam. These include Braille test papers, large-print test papers, exemption from foreign language listening tests, extended exam time, private testing rooms, and permission to bring hearing aids or wheelchairs into the exam hall. These benefits are not automatically granted; candidates must apply in writing by the deadline set by their provincial education authorities, attaching a valid disability certificate (second generation or newer). If a candidate disagrees with the decision, they may request a review from the provincial education department."]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-impact"},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["Cost"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["There is no monetary cost. However, candidates must submit…"]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["Benefit"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["Article 5 of the “Regulations on Managing Accommodations for Disabled Candidates in the National College Entra…"]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-actions","aria-label":"Mark: Disabled candidates taking the national college entrance exam can request reasonable accommodations, including a 50% time extension for those using Braille test papers"},"children":[{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-action done","aria-pressed":"false"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-check","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M20 6 9 17l-5-5"},"children":[]}]},"Done"]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-action todo","aria-pressed":"false"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-list-todo","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"rect","props":{"x":"3","y":"5","width":"6","height":"6","rx":"1"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m3 17 2 2 4-4"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M13 6h8"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M13 12h8"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M13 18h8"},"children":[]}]},"Plan to do"]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-action favorite","aria-pressed":"false"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-bookmark","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m19 21-7-4-7 4V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h10a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v16z"},"children":[]}]},"Save"]}," ",{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"social-share-trigger"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-share2 lucide-share-2","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"18","cy":"5","r":"3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"6","cy":"12","r":"3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"18","cy":"19","r":"3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"line","props":{"x1":"8.59","x2":"15.42","y1":"13.51","y2":"17.49"},"children":[]},{"tag":"line","props":{"x1":"15.41","x2":"8.59","y1":"6.51","y2":"10.49"},"children":[]}]},"Share this tip"]}]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-detail-toggle","aria-expanded":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"10","height":"10","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"currentColor","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-circle","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"12","cy":"12","r":"10"},"children":[]}]},"Hide details"]},{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-chevron-down rotated","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m6 9 6 6 6-6"},"children":[]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-details"},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Cost"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["There is no monetary cost. However, candidates must submit a written application within the timeframe specified by their provincial education authorities and attend an in-person verification session."]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Benefit"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["Article 5 of the “Regulations on Managing Accommodations for Disabled Candidates in the National College Entrance Exam” lists twelve distinct accommodations. These include providing Braille, large-print, or standard test papers for visually impaired students; exempting hearing-impaired students from foreign language listening tests; allowing visually impaired students to bring Braille pens, writing boards, non-recording Braille typewriters, electronic visual aids, white canes, and magnifying glasses into the exam; permitting hearing-impaired students to use hearing aids or cochlear implants; and allowing mobility-limited students to bring wheelchairs or walking aids, with custom desks and chairs available upon request. The time extension is clearly defined in Article 5, Paragraph 6: “For visually impaired candidates using Braille test papers, the total exam time is extended by 50% relative to the standard duration; for those using large-print or standard papers, or for candidates with limited hand mobility due to cerebral palsy or other conditions, the extension is 30%.” Additional benefits include priority access to exam venues, private standardized testing rooms, and on-site assistance from guides and sign language interpreters. Article 7 details the application process: candidates must submit a formal written request by the provincial deadline, accompanied by a valid disability certificate; an expert panel then conducts an on-site assessment, after which the provincial education authority issues a written notice of approval or denial. Article 8 allows candidates to appeal any decision via a written review request to the provincial education department. Article 9 specifies that for candidates exempt from foreign language listening tests, the final score is calculated as “written test score × total foreign language points / total written test points.” Finally, Article 18 states that these same accommodations may be applied to other national education exams, such as graduate school admissions or adult college entrance exams (National Regulations, effective April 7, 2017)."]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Original sources"]},{"tag":"p","props":{"className":"life-citations"},"children":["教育部、中国残联 (2017). 残疾人参加普通高等学校招生全国统一考试管理规定（教学〔2017〕4 号，第五条、第七条、第八条、第九条、第十八条）. ",{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"http://www.gov.cn/zhengce/zhengceku/2017-04/12/content_5650060.htm","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":["http://www.gov.cn/zhengce/zhengceku/2017-04/12/content_5650060.htm"]}]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"http://www.gov.cn/zhengce/zhengceku/2017-04/12/content_5650060.htm","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","className":"life-source-link"},"children":["Open source link"," ",{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"13","height":"13","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-external-link","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M15 3h6v6"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M10 14 21 3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6"},"children":[]}]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Book note"]},{"tag":"p","props":{"className":"life-citations"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-content-reference"},"children":["Each province sets its own application deadline, which is published in its annual college entrance exam registration guidelines. Missing this deadline means no eligibility for accommodations that year. Therefore, students and parents should check their provincial education authority’s website during the first semester of senior year to confirm the exact application window. Article 18 also provides a broader pathway: similar accommodations can be requested for other national education exams, including graduate school and adult college entrance exams. Additionally, Article 14 of this section explicitly prohibits schools from denying enrollment to disabled students. The primary beneficiaries of these provisions are the candidates themselves or their children."]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-personal-note"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["My note"]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button"},"children":["Write a reminder for yourself…"]}]}]}]},{"tag":"nav","props":{"className":"life-tip-pager"},"children":[{"tag":"a","props":{"className":"life-tip-pager-link","href":"/en/tip/33-12"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-arrow-left","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m12 19-7-7 7-7"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M19 12H5"},"children":[]}]},{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"small","props":{},"children":["Previous"]},"Guide dogs are allowed in public places and on public transport; blind individuals ride city buses for free"]}]},{"tag":"a","props":{"className":"life-tip-pager-link next","href":"/en/tip/33-14"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"small","props":{},"children":["Next"]},"Schools may not refuse enrollment for children with disabilities; those unable to attend receive in‑home instruction arranged by the education bureau"]},{"tag"